! D3 ~ the glass engine and the width spike

Order (controller, 2026-10-28): the lane runs on a port a page can reach (D2, PR #103) and on rest-before-reload (PR #91). The operator ruled full as the default on 2026-10-28; the mirror boot lights that width through the D2 port binding, with none as the fallback (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/dreamdom-roadmap">> D3).

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-slices>>

!! The slices, each built red first with its control

# ''G1 ~ the port adaptor ~ BUILT.'' A startup module on the glass (`packages/lararium-tw5/src/glass-port-adaptor.ts`), pure over a `$tw`-shaped wiki and a port transport: it binds `$tw.wiki`'s `change`, lands `port:snapshot` and `port:changes` under an origin tag its own listener skips, posts `port:write` with a `txId`, and keeps the write optimistic until `port:written` echoes; no `$tw.syncer`, no `syncadaptor` module. Skinny and story stand as settings of the same adaptor (`width`, `fields`); skinny asks `port:ask{kind: load}` for a body on open. Witnesses: `glass-echo-lands-once`, `glass-skinny-body-loads-on-open`, `glass-peer-edit-presence-reads-aloud`.
# ''G2 ~ the glass boot and mount ~ BUILT.'' The glass boots `TW5Engine` in the page from the same CAS core blob by hash, mounts the page template over `window.document` in a shadow root as the browser's first camera, through the private mirror door over the explicitly supplied port binding. Skinny opens and paints first, then promotes to full; named failures leave the none floor. `packages/lararium-web/src/glass/`.
# ''G3 ~ the service doors ~ PART.'' `lar:service` doors reached from the glass engine's root handlers (`tm-*`), the same kinds D1 ruled, each refused kind named with its alert.
# ''G4 ~ the multi-tab topology ~ BUILT.'' A Web Lock elects the leader; the leader's worker holds the engine; a SharedWorker or BroadcastChannel handshake routes other tabs; a late tab gets a snapshot, never a missed `ready`. Witnesses: `glass-leader-handoff-mid-write`, `glass-late-tab-gets-snapshot`.
# ''G5 ~ the draft prompt ~ BUILT.'' A peer write into an open draft shows the newer-base prompt; a draft is a tiddler like any other.
# ''G6 ~ the full-width walk ~ PART.'' The five `isTiddlyWikiFakeDom` sites (`FramedEngine`, storyviews, popup positioning, the toolbar, auto-height) walked once in a real browser inside the shadow root; interaction goldens 1 to 13 at width full with stock TW5 as oracle.
# ''G7 ~ the three-boot spike ~ PART.'' One 2,000-tiddler corpus, one loopback port, full, skinny and none (story only if skinny and full split), each measure and threshold the roadmap's D3 Measures states; on this host's browsers and on Node; each phone figure named unmeasured.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/owed>>

!! What stands owed

* ''G3'': the camera builds the scroller, popup layer and focus handler; the `tm-modal`, `tm-notify`, clipboard, download, route and open-surface doors, and `main.ts` calling `standMirror`, stand owed.
* ''G6'': one walk witness runs the framed editor, story scroll, popup layer, toolbar and auto-height in Chromium and Firefox; WebKit refuses on this host for want of two system libraries. Interaction goldens 1 to 13 at width full against stock TW5 stand owed.
* ''G7'' (spike table, 2026-10-28; 2,000 tiddlers, Chromium on this WSL2 host, one loopback relay, median of three runs; every phone figure UNMEASURED): heap after first paint stock 32.18 / full 35.56 / skinny 21.66 MiB; first paint 836 / 942 / 677 ms; keystroke to paint p95 15.1 / 26.5 / 23.7 ms; skinny cold filter p95 3.3 ms; peer write 32 / 43 ms, in order; hot swap 611 / 179 ms; echo one write, zero re-landings; none bytes per key 63,344 against the 52,429-byte budget (phone unmeasured). Full's memory gate reads +10.5 % over stock (tripwire 150 MiB): PASS on this host. The sync ask, the verb census and the none page controls stand unmeasured.
* ''Mirror door'' BUILT: the pool names a mounted wiki's boot inputs (`mountInputsOf`), the browser vessel result carries `mirrorInputs(surface)`, and `main.ts` stands the mirror through `standPageMirror` once the first frame names the surface (host `#mirror`, outcome in `data-lar-mirror`). The operator ruled the mirror the person's visible surface (2026-10-28): that slice moves the edit road, the unload hold and the goldens onto it. The spike re-run on the shipped setup (the island in the tab, not a remote authority over a loopback relay) stands owed.
* ''Promotion order'': skinny paints first and one `port:widen` row promotes it to full; the per-tab `mirror:began` record in `sessionStorage` holds a tab at skinny when a full boot never finished; the order retires on the measured landing cure, not on a date.
* ''Full-width landing cost'' CURED: the 33 s first paint and 106 MiB heap came from an echo storm, not from the adaptor's per-record image or the per-change refresh. A landed record's tag held the wire fields while the change listener read TW5's normalized tiddler (tags, lists and dates rewritten), so every landed record posted itself back as a write (20,227 writes seen); the tag now reads the tiddler back as TW5 holds it. First paint 42,983 to 951 ms, heap 236.34 to 35.56 MiB, writes 20,227 to 102.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-realm>>

!! The mirror's realm ~ the operator's rulings (2026-10-29) as the lane's work order

* ''A page never stands as a vessel.'' The page holds a surface with a port onto a vessel; §9 of the Island Sovereignty Law reads "no sovereign VM and no key on a surface", and the mirror honors it as a camera fed by the port alone.
* ''Browser mode, no lends.'' The mirror boots TW5 in its own browser mode: no `configureIslandRuntime`, no worker boot env, no `global`, `Buffer`, `process`, `setImmediate` or `clearImmediate` lent onto the page window. Mu on the iframe and realm menu (same-origin iframe, sandboxed iframe, ShadowRealm, core patch).
* ''No syncer, no saver, no syncadaptor.'' The port adaptor stays the mirror's one road to truth; TW5's syncer, savers and syncadaptor stay out of its boot, and a person's plugin carrying a syncadaptor or a saver refuses at mount by name.
* ''The surface owns the URL'' through its `route` door; TW5's hash handling stays off and `#:safe` burns. ''Faults'' land on the alert rail, with TW5's `window.onerror` uninstalled. ''Modals and notifications'' paint in the surface's root layer, and `lar-root-services` owns the mirror's doors (G3).
* ''Plugins wait on the seal.'' The full mirror runs people's plugins only after sealed-store steps 2 and 3 land for the browser store; no clear row stands under it, the device key rests non-extractable, and the browser vessel's opened key lives in its own worker.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-fences>>

!! What the lane leaves alone

* The hands spine until PR #108 lands (`session-contract.ts`, `uds-channel.ts`, `uds-session-door.ts`, `session-switch.ts`, `store-door-verbs.ts`, the openers' compose hunks) and I2's `intent-*` files. No opener compose hunk unless the controller hands one; the glass builds it as a named patch.
* The road and the changelog.
* D4's manifest and gate.

<<~/ahu>>

